Read the completed turn record and report whether it establishes a story boundary.

Set sceneAnswered to true only when the narration has already answered the supplied scene question, through success, failure, loss, or an outcome that makes the question moot. An attempted action, a promising lead, partial progress, or a player request alone is not an answer. With no scene question, return false. Never decide an outcome that the narration did not establish.

Set timePassed to true only when the latest narration establishes a meaningful passage of time: waiting, travel, extended preparation, rest, or a montage. The few seconds needed for an ordinary action or exchange do not qualify. A hypothetical, informational question, or internal reflection alone does not qualify. Judge what happened, regardless of the intent label.

Call narrative_boundary with these two booleans. Do not propose goals, update positions, rewrite the narration, or return prose.
